msgstr "Semua node intermediate (lingkaran) bertugas melakukan berbagai jenis manipulasi data.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Query the required inputs and expected outputs {#query-the-required-inputs-and-expected-outputs}"
msgstr "Mengkueri input yang diperlukan dan output yang diharapkan {#query-the-required-inputs-and-expected-outputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The easiest way to see the required inputs and expected outputs is to print the [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") object. Array items are formatted as `'{name}' <{type}[{shape}...]>`, and the required inputs precede the optional inputs.\n"
msgstr "Cara termudah untuk melihat input yang diperlukan dan output yang diharapkan adalah dengan mencetak objek [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\"). Item array diformat sebagai `'{name}' <{type}[{shape}...]>`, dan input yang wajib ditampilkan sebelum input opsional.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") and [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") of the samplex, as well as more detailed information like their names, shapes, types, and descriptions, can also be queried programatically. The return type of both of these methods is a [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"). For example, the following code lists all specifications of the input interface:\n"
msgstr "[`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") dan [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") dari samplex, serta informasi yang lebih rinci seperti nama, shape, tipe, dan deskripsinya, juga bisa dikueri secara programatik. Tipe kembalian kedua method ini adalah [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"). Misalnya, kode berikut mencantumkan semua spesifikasi antarmuka input:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next example prints some information about those output specifiers whose names contain the string `\"flips\"`.\n"
msgstr "Contoh berikutnya mencetak beberapa informasi tentang specifier output yang namanya mengandung string `\"flips\"`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bind input values and sample {#bind-input-values-and-sample}"
msgstr "Bind nilai input dan sampling {#bind-input-values-and-sample}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), the samplex needs values for at least those [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") that are marked as required. These values are first bound to an input interface so that it can perform all necessary type checking (or type coercion in some cases) and shape analysis. If anything is wrong with the types or shapes, or if a required value is missing, a verbose error is raised.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melakukan [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), samplex memerlukan nilai untuk setidaknya [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") yang ditandai wajib. Nilai-nilai ini pertama-tama di-bind ke antarmuka input agar antarmuka itu bisa melakukan semua pemeriksaan tipe (atau koersi tipe dalam beberapa kasus) dan analisis shape. Kalau ada yang salah pada tipe atau shape, atau ada nilai wajib yang hilang, error yang rinci akan dimunculkan.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bind input {#bind-input}"
msgstr "Mengikat input {#bind-input}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following example, the [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") method is passed the required input values. It is then used to draw three randomizations from the samplex. The required bindings from the dressings are the Pauli Lindblad maps for noise injection and the basis change array. Additionally, values for the four parameters in the original boxed circuit are required, which in this case is set to `np.linspace(0, 1, 4)`. The samplex composes these parameters into the dressings, so they effectively become modifications to the samplex’s output parameter values.\n"
msgstr "Pada contoh berikut, method [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") diberi nilai input yang wajib. Method ini lalu dipakai untuk menarik tiga pengacakan dari samplex. Binding wajib dari dressing adalah peta Pauli Lindblad untuk injeksi noise dan array basis change. Selain itu, nilai untuk keempat parameter pada circuit asli yang sudah di-box juga diperlukan, yang dalam kasus ini diatur ke `np.linspace(0, 1, 4)`. Samplex menggabungkan parameter ini ke dalam dressing, sehingga secara efektif parameter itu menjadi modifikasi pada nilai parameter output samplex.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inputs can be bound to the interface through multiple calls to [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") or by direct item assignment. Despite the nested dictionary format that [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") allows for convenience, it is a flat mapping object, and supports all of the usual mapping syntax. Once all required inputs have been found, [`fully_bound`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound\") becomes true.\n"
msgstr "Input bisa di-bind ke antarmuka lewat beberapa kali panggilan [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") atau lewat penugasan item langsung. Meskipun [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") menerima format dictionary bersarang demi kemudahan, objeknya adalah mapping datar, dan mendukung semua sintaks mapping yang biasa. Begitu semua input wajib sudah ditemukan, [`fully_bound`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound\") menjadi true.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") objects, including the [`SamplexOutput`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex-output#samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput \"samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput\") subclass, map objects against data that has been bound to them. This means that you can get, for example, the template parameter values as follows. In this case, it has shape `(3, 48)` since three randomizations were requested and the template circuit has 48 parameters.\n"
msgstr "Semua objek [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"), termasuk subclass [`SamplexOutput`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex-output#samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput \"samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput\"), memetakan objek terhadap data yang sudah di-bind ke dalamnya. Artinya, kamu bisa mendapatkan, misalnya, nilai parameter template seperti berikut. Dalam kasus ini, shape-nya `(3, 48)` karena tiga pengacakan diminta dan template circuit punya 48 parameter.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify input as a dictionary {#specify-input-as-a-dictionary}"
msgstr "Menentukan input sebagai dictionary {#specify-input-as-a-dictionary}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of providing a fully-bound [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"), you can specify the inputs as a standard dictionary, as is shown in the cell below. In this case, the [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") method internally binds the dictionary items to the samplex’s input interface to validate that all required inputs are present and compatible.\n"
msgstr "Alih-alih memberikan [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") yang sudah di-bind sepenuhnya, kamu bisa menentukan input sebagai dictionary standar, seperti pada cell di bawah. Dalam kasus ini, method [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") secara internal mem-bind item dictionary ke antarmuka input samplex untuk memvalidasi bahwa semua input wajib ada dan kompatibel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Input types {#input-types}"
msgstr "Tipe input {#input-types}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Currently, there are two interface value types:\n"
msgstr "Saat ini ada dua tipe nilai antarmuka:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Array-valued: These have a shape and a data type. Bound values are coerced into the data type if possible. Any dimension can be a free dimension.\n"
msgstr "Bernilai array: Ini punya shape dan tipe data. Nilai yang di-bind dikoersi ke tipe data tersebut kalau memungkinkan. Dimensi mana pun bisa menjadi dimensi bebas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli Lindblad maps: These must be of type [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) and must act on the prescribed number of qubits. The number of terms in the map is a free dimension.\n"
msgstr "Peta Pauli Lindblad: Ini harus bertipe [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) dan harus bekerja pada jumlah qubit yang ditentukan. Jumlah suku dalam peta adalah dimensi bebas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Free dimensions {#free-dimensions}"
msgstr "Dimensi bebas {#free-dimensions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") class has a notion of *free dimensions*, which are named integer sizes whose values are undetermined until some data has been bound to the interface that constrains them. All free dimensions of the same name must resolve to a consistent size when binding data, or an error will be raised. For example, in the [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") of any samplex, the array axis corresponding to randomizations is a free parameter that has the name `\"num_randomizations\"` by convention. When `sample()` is called, it binds values to the outputs\n"
msgstr "Kelas [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") punya konsep *dimensi bebas*, yaitu ukuran bilangan bulat bernama yang nilainya belum ditentukan sampai ada data yang di-bind ke antarmuka dan membatasinya. Semua dimensi bebas dengan nama yang sama harus menghasilkan ukuran yang konsisten saat data di-bind, kalau tidak, error akan dimunculkan. Misalnya, pada [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") dari samplex mana pun, sumbu array yang sesuai dengan pengacakan adalah parameter bebas yang secara konvensi bernama `\"num_randomizations\"`. Saat `sample()` dipanggil, ia mem-bind nilai ke output\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Another common free-dimension scenario is sharing term constraints between Pauli lindblad map specifications and their modifiers. A [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) is an ordered sequence of terms, where each term contains a floating point rate and a sparse Pauli representation. The [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function adds a specifier `\"pauli_lindblad_maps.<ref>\"` for this type for each [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation, and if it contains a `modifier_ref`, a `\"local_scales.<modifier_ref>\"` specifier is also added. Both of these share the free dimension `\"num_terms_<ref>\"` that specifies how many Pauli Lindblad terms are present in the noise model because the latter needs to zip against the rates of the former to scale them.\n"
msgstr "Skenario dimensi bebas umum lainnya adalah berbagi batasan suku antara spesifikasi peta Pauli lindblad dan pengubahnya. [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) adalah urutan suku yang terurut, di mana setiap suku berisi laju floating point dan representasi Pauli yang sparse. Fungsi [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") menambahkan specifier `\"pauli_lindblad_maps.<ref>\"` untuk tipe ini bagi setiap anotasi [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\"), dan kalau anotasi itu punya `modifier_ref`, specifier `\"local_scales.<modifier_ref>\"` juga ditambahkan. Keduanya berbagi dimensi bebas `\"num_terms_<ref>\"` yang menentukan berapa banyak suku Pauli Lindblad yang ada dalam model noise, karena yang belakangan perlu di-zip dengan laju yang pertama untuk menskalakannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qubit-ordering-convention\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qubit ordering convention {#qubit-ordering-convention}"
msgstr "Konvensi urutan qubit {#qubit-ordering-convention}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplexes constructed from boxed circuits by the [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function can require array-valued inputs to [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), where one index corresponds to qubits in a circuit’s box. This section explains the ordering convention that should be used for such axes. In summary: use the qubit order of the boxed circuit, restricted to the box’s qubits.\n"
msgstr "Samplex yang dibangun dari circuit ber-box oleh fungsi [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") bisa memerlukan input bernilai array ke [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), di mana satu indeks sesuai dengan qubit di dalam box circuit. Bagian ini menjelaskan konvensi urutan yang harus dipakai untuk sumbu semacam itu. Singkatnya: pakai urutan qubit dari circuit yang di-box, dibatasi pada qubit milik box.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, suppose you want to figure out how to specify a Pauli Lindblad map for `\"noise1\"`. Then the order of qubits in the noise map is with respect to these qubits:\n"
msgstr "Misalnya, kamu ingin tahu cara menentukan peta Pauli Lindblad untuk `\"noise1\"`. Maka urutan qubit dalam peta noise mengacu pada qubit-qubit berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, if you want `<Qubit register=(4, \"q0\"), index=2>` to be noisy with `X` noise, then you should define a Pauli Lindblad map like this one because it is at index `1` of `qubit_ordering_convention`.\n"
msgstr "Artinya, kalau kamu ingin `<Qubit register=(4, \"q0\"), index=2>` mengalami noise `X`, maka kamu harus mendefinisikan peta Pauli Lindblad seperti ini karena qubit itu berada di indeks `1` dari `qubit_ordering_convention`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same holds true for basis changes. If you want to rotate into the +1 eigenstates of the operators X, Y, and Z for qubits 0, 1, and 2 of `circuit`, respectively, then you should use the following array, recalling that the convention $I=0$, $Z=1$, $X=2$, and $Y=3$ is used in this library (and Qiskit).\n"
msgstr "Hal yang sama berlaku untuk basis change. Kalau kamu ingin merotasi ke eigenstate +1 dari operator X, Y, dan Z untuk qubit 0, 1, dan 2 dari `circuit`, secara berurutan, maka kamu harus memakai array berikut, dengan mengingat bahwa library ini (dan Qiskit) memakai konvensi $I=0$, $Z=1$, $X=2$, dan $Y=3$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the qubit ordering convention is *not* the order defined by either of the following:\n"
msgstr "Perlu diingat bahwa konvensi urutan qubit *bukan* urutan yang didefinisikan oleh salah satu dari berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`box_instruction.qubits`, where `box_instruction` is a [`qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction) whose operation is a [`qiskit.circuit.BoxOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.BoxOp), because the order of this list of qubits might depend on the order in which instructions were added to the box context, which would be a confusing convention. For example, `with box(): circuit.x([0, 1])` and `with box(): circuit.x([1, 0])` would result in different orderings.\n"
msgstr "`box_instruction.qubits`, di mana `box_instruction` adalah [`qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction) yang operasinya adalah [`qiskit.circuit.BoxOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.BoxOp), karena urutan daftar qubit ini bisa bergantung pada urutan instruksi ditambahkan ke konteks box, yang akan menjadi konvensi yang membingungkan. Misalnya, `with box(): circuit.x([0, 1])` dan `with box(): circuit.x([1, 0])` akan menghasilkan urutan yang berbeda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`box_instruction.operation.body.qubits` because these qubits might not even appear in the outer circuit. Qubits inside the actual body of `BoxOp` instructions (or any other control flow operation like `IfElseOp`) are only promised to have a consisent meaning within that scope. This would be an ill-defined convention, and hard to use in general.\n"
msgstr "`box_instruction.operation.body.qubits` karena qubit-qubit ini bahkan mungkin tidak muncul di circuit luar. Qubit di dalam body instruksi `BoxOp` yang sebenarnya (atau operasi control flow lain seperti `IfElseOp`) hanya dijamin punya makna yang konsisten dalam scope itu. Ini akan menjadi konvensi yang tidak terdefinisi dengan baik dan sulit dipakai secara umum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Local testing with the template circuit {#local-testing-with-the-template-circuit}"
msgstr "Pengujian lokal dengan template circuit {#local-testing-with-the-template-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") is constructed by using the [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function, the output parameter values should be directly compatible with the parameters of the associated template circuit. For example, you can bind values for one of the randomizations to the template for local inspection.\n"
msgstr "Kalau sebuah [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") dibangun dengan fungsi [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\"), nilai parameter output seharusnya langsung kompatibel dengan parameter template circuit yang terkait. Misalnya, kamu bisa mem-bind nilai untuk salah satu pengacakan ke template untuk diperiksa secara lokal.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lets you verify that the samplex is outputing samples that are expected. For example, the following code casts the bound circuit to a [`qiskit.quantum_info.Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) object and composes with the bitflip Paulis to visually inspect that all three randomizations are logically equivalent to the base circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ini memungkinkan kamu memverifikasi bahwa samplex menghasilkan sampel yang diharapkan. Misalnya, kode berikut mengubah circuit yang sudah di-bind menjadi objek [`qiskit.quantum_info.Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) dan menggabungkannya dengan Pauli bitflip untuk memeriksa secara visual bahwa ketiga pengacakan secara logis setara dengan circuit dasar.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, the following code passes output parameter values and the template to a sampler to simulate 10,000 shots of all randomizations, and compares the resulting expectation values (only of the alpha register) to the expectation values of a base circuit simulation.\n"
msgstr "Demikian pula, kode berikut meneruskan nilai parameter output dan template ke sampler untuk mensimulasikan 10.000 shot dari semua pengacakan, lalu membandingkan nilai ekspektasi yang dihasilkan (hanya dari register alpha) dengan nilai ekspektasi dari simulasi circuit dasar.\n"
